    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64980,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lateral walls of the vagina</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64981,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients present with abnormal vaginal bleeding or a vaginal mass {6137744; 18028380; 29970606; 15105647}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64982,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are extremely rare vaginal neoplasms.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64983,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64984,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>Mesonephric adenocarcinomas of the vagina arise from vaginal mesonephric remnants. See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/175\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Adenocarcinoma, HPV-independent, mesonephric type, of the uterine cervix</em>, which has the same derivation.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T13:55:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64985,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The macroscopic features are those of a mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64986,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Mesonephric adenocarcinoma typically exhibits various architectural patterns (including tubular, ductal, solid, papillary, retiform, and sex cord&ndash;like) within the same tumour. Eosinophilic luminal material may be present. The solid foci may be partly or entirely spindled and may contain heterologous elements, such as cartilage. The cells are usually cuboidal or columnar, with eosinophilic cytoplasm. The nuclei often have irregular nuclear membranes and grooves, and nuclear pseudoinclusions may be seen. Mesonephric remnants may be seen in the background.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemically, there is usually positivity for pancytokeratins, CD10 (apical/luminal staining), EMA, and PAX8 {22456609; 12548163; 12877729}. GATA3, TTF1, and calretinin are variably positive {22456609; 26135559; 11224609}. ER and PR are usually completely negative {22456609; 11224609}. p16 is negative or patchy/weak and HPV is negative {22456609}.</p>\r\n<p>Refer also to <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/175\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Adenocarcinoma, HPV-independent, mesonephric type, of the uterine cervix</em>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T13:55:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64987,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/175\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Adenocarcinoma, HPV-independent, mesonephric type, of the uterine cervix</em>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T13:55:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64988,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No vaginal mesonephric carcinomas have been studied at the molecular level; however, cervical mesonephric carcinomas have characteristic molecular alterations, most notably <em>KRAS</em> mutations {26336887}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64989,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> admixture of architectural patterns.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> association with adjacent mesonephric remnants and/or mesonephric hyperplasia; positivity for CD10, GATA3, and/or TTF1; negativity for ER/PR and napsin&nbsp;A; HPV negativity.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-26T14:50:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64990,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is the same as for other vaginal neoplasms.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64991,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Prognosis and prediction are unknown because of the limited number of cases described in the literature.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:10:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]